RoboDog: raise the ES7210 mic PGA on the RLCD-4.2 board (#301).

`adc_init_gain: 0` left the board's capture at 0 dB PGA: the USB test dongle
(plugged into the bench host, speaker ~cm from the board mic) put the corpus
only ~11 dB above the mic's noise floor, far under the RT VAD threshold
(mean-abs > 300) and unintelligible to ASR.  esp_codec_dev's es7210 maps this
dB value through get_db() to GAIN_0DB..GAIN_37_5DB; 30 dB is a supported step.
Applied by build_esp_claw.sh over the pristine upstream board file (do not
vendor that file into the repo).

--- a/application/edge_agent/boards/waveshare/waveshare_ESP32_S3_RLCD_4_2/board_devices.yaml
+++ b/application/edge_agent/boards/waveshare/waveshare_ESP32_S3_RLCD_4_2/board_devices.yaml
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
       adc_max_channel: 4
       # Bit0=Mic0, Bit1=Mic1(ref), Bit2=Mic2, Bit3=Mic3 — dual mic + reference
       adc_channel_mask: "0011"
-      adc_init_gain: 0          # dB
+      adc_init_gain: 30         # dB (RoboDog: ES7210 PGA; 0 dB left the corpus under the VAD floor, #301)
     peripherals:
       - name: i2s_audio_in
       - name: i2c_master
